# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true and deployed to Linux
# via `git archive HEAD | ssh ... tar xzf -`. Without this file, git archive applies
# the autocrlf filter and every shell script arrives on the server with CRLF, where
# `set -euo pipefail\r` fails with "invalid option name" and every variable carries a
# trailing CR. That silently breaks the nightly backup cron — verified 2026-07-28 by
# diffing `git show HEAD:deploy/backup.sh` (LF) against `git archive HEAD` (CRLF).
#
# Anything the server executes or parses must be LF.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
